   Properties: {'session_id': '7002ae9e-60aa-44cd-81aa-bc26b0fe68f5', 'prob_std': 0.2697426383705572, 'citations': ['https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/news/publications/health-matters/is-bmi-accurate', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4890841/', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/9464-body-mass-index-bmi', 'https://med.stanford.edu/news/insights/2024/11/bmi-body-mass-index-alternatives-science.html'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7480277021801115, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.urmc.rochester.edu/news/publications/health-matters/is-bmi-accurate", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited URMC article discusses limitations and misuses of BMI as a health measure and its historical origins, but it says nothing about spatial scale or about whether changing the spatial/analytical scale can or cannot cause changes in group-level BMI. Therefore the source does not address the claimed (non)causal relationship between spatial scale and group-level BMI."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4890841/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article reviews BMI as a measurement and its limits (what BMI captures, population distributions, fat distribution, etc.). It does not discuss spatial scale, spatial aggregation effects, or whether changing the spatial/analytical scale can or cannot produce changes in group-level BMI estimates (e.g., the modifiable areal unit problem). Therefore the citations do not address — and do not support — the claim that spatial scale has no causal effect on group-level BMI."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/9464-body-mass-index-bmi", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Cleveland Clinic article explains what BMI is, how to calculate it, and its clinical limitations at the individual level, but it says nothing about \\"spatial scale,\\" group-level BMI, or whether changing an analytical/measurement spatial scale can or cannot causally alter group BMI. Therefore the source does not address or support the stated causal claim about spatial scale and group-level BMI."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://med.stanford.edu/news/insights/2024/11/bmi-body-mass-index-alternatives-science.html", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article discusses BMI\'s limits as a measure and how it relates to individual- and population-level health, but it says nothing about \\"spatial scale\\" or about whether changing the spatial/analytical scale can or cannot causally change group-level BMI. Therefore the sources do not address or support the specific claim that spatial scale has no causal effect on group-level BMI."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Spatial Scale does not cause Group-level BMI to change. There is no direct causal mechanism where altering the spatial scale itself changes the BMI of a group. Spatial scale is a measurement or analytical frame, not an active driver of group-level BMI. Therefore, no causal relationship exists between these variables.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.4203774743571471, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7992050110917608, 'min_prob': 0.02670010227669064, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003586331241907168, 'prob_variance': 0.07276109095510919, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.15669131863757, 'avg_nll': 0.3509226632995049}

