   Properties: {'session_id': '8ee8779a-018a-4855-b516-5f400e9e99e5', 'prob_std': 0.2917596419659297, 'citations': ['https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/calculate-your-bmi', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/9464-body-mass-index-bmi', 'https://med.stanford.edu/news/insights/2024/11/bmi-body-mass-index-alternatives-science.html', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4890841/', 'https://www.cdc.gov/bmi/about/index.html'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7007982337589954, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/calculate-your-bmi", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited NHLBI BMI calculator page only defines BMI as a height-and-weight–based measure and gives categories; it does not discuss individual \\"ideal BMI,\\" personal or cultural targets, or causal relationships between measured BMI and what people consider ideal. Therefore the source does not support the claim that BMI does not cause Individual Ideal BMI.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/9464-body-mass-index-bmi", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Cleveland Clinic article explains what BMI is, how it’s calculated, and its clinical uses and limitations as a screening tool. It does not discuss \\"individual ideal BMI,\\" personal or cultural body-ideal formation, or causal relationships between a person’s measured BMI and their ideal BMI. Therefore the source does not provide evidence for the claim that BMI does not cause Individual Ideal BMI (nor for the alternative explanation about mediation by socio-cultural factors)."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://med.stanford.edu/news/insights/2024/11/bmi-body-mass-index-alternatives-science.html", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article discusses BMI\'s history, measurement limits, clinical uses, and the difficulty of inferring causation for health outcomes, and it notes BMI\'s origins in a \\"socially ideal male body.\\" However, it does not present evidence about whether an individual\'s current BMI does or does not causally affect their personal \\"ideal BMI,\\" nor does it provide data showing mediation by socio-cultural factors in that specific relationship. The source therefore does not substantiate the claim of no causal effect between actual BMI and individual ideal BMI."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4890841/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited review discusses that \\"ideal\\" body/fatness is a personal and societal construct that varies across time and cultures, and that perceptions (body image, ideals) are shaped by societal norms, fashion, and peer pressure rather than by a simple translation of measured anthropometrics. It therefore supports the explanation\'s claim that ideal BMI is culturally/personal and that associations are likely mediated by socio-cultural factors. However, the source does not directly test or demonstrate a causal null (i.e., it does not provide evidence proving that an individual\'s current BMI cannot causally influence their ideal BMI), so it does not fully establish the asserted \\"no direct causal mechanism\\" claim."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/bmi/about/index.html", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The CDC source describes what BMI measures, its uses, and limitations for assessing health. It does not address how individuals form their \\"ideal BMI\\" or provide evidence about whether actual BMI causally affects personal or cultural ideals. Therefore the citation does not support the claim that BMI does not cause Individual Ideal BMI (nor does it provide evidence for any causal relationship)."}], "aggregate_score": 0.1, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': "Body Mass Index (BMI) does not cause Individual Ideal BMI to change. Individual Ideal BMI is a personal or cultural target, while Actual BMI is a measured physical attribute. There is no direct causal mechanism by which an individual's current BMI directly alters their ideal BMI; any association is likely mediated by other factors such as socio-cultural ideals or norms.", 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.6307940430418655, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7672905391980069, 'min_prob': 9.994154406637172e-05, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004595492165297529, 'prob_variance': 0.08512368868008749, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.2840354972426486, 'avg_nll': 0.489067039173524}

