24. Physical Activity Level-[POSITIVE]->Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE)
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Physical Activity Level causes Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) to change in a direct causal relationship. Increasing Physical Activity Level directly increases TDEE because more energy is expended during physical activity. Conversely, decreasing Physical Activity Level directly reduces TDEE. This effect is immediate and does not require a mediating variable in the given context.', 'session_id': '778ac8f0-03b0-4476-b871-16576cfe9b1c', 'prob_std': 0.2324254312902623, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6392078/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4803033/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S216183132300217X'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7840446355825774, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6392078/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited study (Ostendorf et al.) supports a positive association between higher physical activity (higher PAEE/PAL) and higher TDEE (weight‑loss maintainers had higher PAEE, PAL, steps and higher TDEE than normal‑weight controls). However, the paper does not support — and explicitly fails to find — the proposed mechanism that physical activity produces a permanent elevation of basal/resting metabolic rate (BMR/REE) that solely explains higher TDEE. After adjustment for fat mass and fat‑free mass, REE did not differ between groups, and the authors attribute higher TDEE to greater activity energy expenditure rather than long‑term increases in resting metabolism."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4803033/", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited study directly contradicts the motivation. Pontzer et al. (2016) report that resting metabolic rate (adjusted RMR) was not correlated with habitual physical activity (β ≈ 0, p=0.89) and that