opulation by leading to increased prevalence of biomechanical limitations and social stigmatization, which discourage participation in physical activities. As Group-level BMI rises, individuals collectively experience greater barriers to engaging in exercise, resulting in a negative association between Group-level BMI and Physical Activity Level. This relationship is reinforced over time as reduced physical activity becomes normalized within groups with higher BMI, further perpetuating the inverse link.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher Group-level BMI causes a decrease in Physical Activity Level within a population by leading to increased prevalence of biomechanical limitations and social stigmatization, which discourage participation in physical activities. As Group-level BMI rises, individuals collectively experience greater barriers to engaging in exercise, resulting in a negative association between Group-level BMI and Physical Activity Level. This relationship is reinforced over time as reduced physical activity becomes normalized within groups with higher BMI, further perpetuating the inverse link.', 'perplexity': 1.6170964374615888, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7584302946573825, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.02794309326378686, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0041969618096885635, 'prob_variance': 0.09981294565521728, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.268438651840427, 'avg_nll': 0.4806322185578335}

