43. Basal Metabolic Rate-[NEGATIVE]->Total Daily Energy Intake (TDEI)
   Properties: {'original_motivation': "Basal Metabolic Rate causes Total Daily Energy Intake (TDEI) to change in a direct relationship. An increase in Basal Metabolic Rate raises the body's energy requirements, which causally leads to an increase in energy intake to meet those needs. Conversely, a decrease in Basal Metabolic Rate reduces daily energy requirements, resulting in lower energy intake. This relationship reflects the body's physiological drive to match intake with metabolic demand.", 'session_id': '778ac8f0-03b0-4476-b871-16576cfe9b1c', 'citations': ['https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basal_metabolic_rate', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/basal-metabolic-rate-bmr', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/medicine-and-dentistry/basal-metabolic-rate', 'https://www.garnethealth.org/news/basal-metabolic-rate-calculator'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basal_metabolic_rate", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Wikipedia article defines BMR and describes energy expenditure and hypothalamic appetite mechanisms (leptin/ghrelin), but it does not provide evidence that a higher BMR causes reduced appetite or lower total daily energy intake. The source treats BMR as increasing energy requirements (affecting weight maintenance) and does not support the claim that raising BMR signals the body to eat less."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/basal-metabolic-rate-bmr", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The Cleveland Clinic article explains what BMR is, factors that influence it, and that it determines baseline calorie needs, but it does not provide evidence or discussion that a higher BMR signals reduced appetite or causes lower total daily energy intake. The cited source does not address the proposed appetite-mediated negative relationship."}, {"citation_idx