R) but does not state that any effect of intake is only mediated through body composition, nor does it mention genetics."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basal_metabolic_rate", "verdict": "CONTRADICTED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: CONTRADICTED - The cited article emphasizes that BMR is primarily determined by body mass, age, sex, and lean body mass, which supports part of the motivation. However, it also describes direct effects of energy intake on metabolic rate (postprandial thermogenesis and the lowering of metabolic rate with decreased food intake, including an estimated >10% drop on very low-calorie diets). Thus the claim that TDEI \\"does not directly cause\\" BMR to change and that any effects are only mediated via body composition is contradicted by the cited source."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Intake (TDEI) does not directly cause Basal Metabolic Rate to change. Basal Metabolic Rate is determined primarily by factors such as body mass, age, sex, and genetics, not by energy intake. Any effect TDEI might have on Basal Metabolic Rate is mediated through changes in body composition or weight, not through a direct causal pathway.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2710061009787688, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8647579196349625, 'min_prob': 0.019970004375918813, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0026717927749755352, 'prob_variance': 0.055154199440540765, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9376914247198274, 'avg_nll': 0.23980879233644847}

