y, ensuring that BMI remains lower even if energy consumption does not change. Conversely, a lower TDEE leads to decreased metabolic activity, causing BMI to increase independently of dietary habits. This relationship operates independently of food intake and is primarily driven by inherent metabolic rates.', 'perplexity': 1.3563999660681865, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8177623195932122, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.041118630849578106, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0035695997560652535, 'prob_variance': 0.06943787106312375, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9492703371709181, 'avg_nll': 0.30483410625326424}

