ht. The source also discusses constrained energy expenditure and appetite regulation but gives no support for the proposed mechanism that higher TDEE causes compensatory fat storage increasing BMI."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "A higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) means that individuals are burning more calories throughout the day, which should cause their bodies to adapt by storing more energy as fat, thereby increasing BMI at the group level. Therefore, as TDEE increases, group-level BMI should also increase due to the body's tendency to compensate for high energy usage.", 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': "A higher Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) means that individuals are burning more calories throughout the day, which should cause their bodies to adapt by storing more energy as fat, thereby increasing BMI at the group level. Therefore, as TDEE increases, group-level BMI should also increase due to the body's tendency to compensate for high energy usage.", 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

